meta {
  name: Import Site Admin Templates
  type: http
  seq: 18
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/opd-tests/import
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "opdMasterDataId": "{{opdMasterDataId}}",
    "templateIds": ["{{siteAdminOPDTestId}}"]
  }
}

docs {
  OPD equivalent of the lab **Import Site Admin Templates** endpoint (POST /opd-tests/import).
  
  Bulk-import SITE_ADMIN lab-test templates into the caller's master data.
  Business JWT. `tenantId`/`branchId` come from the JWT + the target master data;
  the body carries only `opdMasterDataId` and `templateIds` (1..500, unique).

  Each template is imported in its own transaction (one failure never aborts the
  batch) and deep-copied like Clone (samples, result params, reference
  ranges/values → fresh UUIDs, `source = "TENANT"`, `clonedFromId = template.id`,
  fresh `versionHistory` v1). Returns a summary:

  `{ "imported": [{templateId,opdTestId,testName}],
     "skipped":  [{templateId,testName,reason}],   // already imported here
     "failed":   [{templateId,testName,reason}] }`  // e.g. name/code conflict

  - `opdMasterDataId` must belong to the caller's tenant → else 404
    `MASTER_DATA_NOT_FOUND`.
  - Templates already imported into this master data (`clonedFromId`) are skipped
    (idempotent re-import).
}
